  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#37859\", \"PowerToys#46873\"], \"answer\": \"This crash has been reported before. The canonical ticket is PowerToys#37859, and PowerToys#46873 was closed as a duplicate of it. The stack trace is the same: a NullReferenceException in BindingExpression.SetupDefaultValueConverter, raised while WPF handles a system theme change (ThemeManager.OnSystemThemeChanged). In those reports it happened after waking from sleep or hibernation, or after a display or dock change. The original reporter said it was a one-time crash, and the tickets I read give no fix or workaround. Restart PowerToys, which should recover from it. Please add your details to #37859: your version (0.98.1.0), what you were doing when it crashed, and whether it happens again. If it does, attach the PowerToys bug report ZIP and the PowerToys Run log file.\"}",
